3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17-vhrm-4-0893"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rouser</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Fleischer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Yamamoto</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>1970</year><article-title>Two dimensional thin layer chromatographic separation of polar lipids and determination of phospholipids by phosphorous analysis of spots</article-title><source>Lipids</source><volume>5</volume><fpage>494</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5483450</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18-vhrm-4-0893"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sampietro</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Lenzi</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Cecchetti</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1986</year><article-title>Nonenzymatic glycation of human platelet membrane proteins in vitro and in vivo</article-title><source>Clin Chem</source><volume>32</volume><fpage>1328</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3719941</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b19-vhrm-4-0893"><citation citation-type="book"><collab>Stedman&#x02019;s (ed)</collab><year>2005</year><article-title>Stedman's Medical Dictionary for the Health Professional and Nursing</article-title><edition>5th ed</edition><publisher-loc>Baltimore</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Lippincott, Williams and Wilkins</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b20-vhrm-4-0893"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Talwar</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Srivastava</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Textbook of Biochemistry and Human Biology</article-title><publisher-loc>New Delhi</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Prentice Hall of India</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="b21-vhrm-4-0893"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Valabhji</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Elkeles</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Dyslipidemia in type 2 diabetes: Epidemiology and biochemistry</article-title><source>Br J Diabetes Vasc Dis</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>184</fpage><lpage>9</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b22-vhrm-4-0893"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Watala</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Pluta</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Golanski</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Increased protein glycation in diabetes mellitus is associated with decreased aspirin-mediated protein acetylation and reduced sensitivity of blood platelets to aspirin</article-title><source>J Mol Med</source><volume>83</volume><fpage>148</fpage><lpage>58</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15723265</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b23-vhrm-4-0893"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Watala</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><year>1988</year><article-title>In vitro glycation of red blood cell proteins: high levels of glucose lower lipid fluidity of erythrocyte membranes</article-title><source>Exp Pathol</source><volume>33</volume><fpage>233</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3229458</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b24-vhrm-4-0893"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>[WHO] World Health Organization</collab></person-group><year>2007</year>What is diabetes? (updated 2006) [online]. Accessed on November 14, 2007. URL: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.who.int/mediacentre/factsheets/fs312/en/index.html">http://www. who.int/mediacentre/factsheets/fs312/en/index.html</ext-link></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="f1-vhrm-4-0893" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Graph showing membrane cholesterol means amongst the three groups.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="vhrm-4-0893f1"/></fig><fig id="f2-vhrm-4-0893" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Graph showing red blood cell (RBC) membrane phospholipids means amongst the three groups.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="vhrm-4-0893f2"/></fig><fig id="f3-vhrm-4-0893" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Graph showing comparison between systolic blood pressure (BP) and waist/hip ratio means amongst the three groups.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="vhrm-4-0893f3"/></fig><fig id="f4-vhrm-4-0893" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Graph showing serum cholesterol means amongst the three groups.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="vhrm-4-0893f4"/></fig><fig id="f5-vhrm-4-0893" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Graph showing comparison between serum cholesterol and red blood cell membrane cholesterol means amongst the three groups.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="vhrm-4-0893f5"/></fig><fig id="f6-vhrm-4-0893" position="float"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Graph showing comparison between HDL and LDL means amongst the three groups.</p><p><bold>Abbreviations:</bold> HDL, high-density lipoprotein; LDL, low-density lipoprotein.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="vhrm-4-0893f6"/></fig><table-wrap id="t1-vhrm-4-0893" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Means and standard deviations for the variables tested for controls, diabetics and diabetics with nephropathy</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Variable</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Controls(Mean &#x000b1; SD) n = 20</th><th align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diabetics (Mean &#x000b1; SD) n = 20</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diabetes with nephropathy(Mean &#x000b1; SD) n = 20</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Body mass index (Kg/m<sup>2</sup>)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">24.67 &#x000b1; 5.18</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">28.17 &#x000b1; 4.98</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">25.87 &#x000b1; 4.68</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Waist/hip ratio</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.85 &#x000b1; 0.06</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.87 &#x000b1; 0.07</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.91 &#x000b1; 0.07</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Systolic blood pressure(mmHg)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">119.15 &#x000b1; 13.03</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">153.21 &#x000b1; 22.10</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">158.60 &#x000b1; 22.49</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Diastolic blood pressure(mmHg)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">76.80 &#x000b1; 7.65</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">94.93 &#x000b1; 10.62</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">90.30 &#x000b1; 13.61</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Glucose (mg/100 mL)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">83.25 &#x000b1; 6.29</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">120.55 &#x000b1; 41.20</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">105.20 &#x000b1; 37.64</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>